### Survival quantiles

`predict_median()` is really a shortcut for `predict_quantile(p=0.5)`. Call `predict_quantile()`
directly with a list of probabilities to get several survival-time quantiles at once, still in
closed form and still with confidence intervals available.

::: {#a5f18c7a .cell execution_count=18}
``` {.python .cell-code}
# Predicted survival-time quantiles at the 25th, 50th, and 75th percentiles
aft.predict_quantile(newdata, p=[0.25, 0.5, 0.75], format="polars")
```

