Royston-Parmar models also support `predict_median()`, which finds the time at which the smooth
survival curve crosses 0.5 via root-finding on the spline. Confidence intervals use the delta method
on the log cumulative hazard.

::: {#a6e3eb1c .cell execution_count=29}
``` {.python .cell-code}
# Median survival time from the Royston-Parmar model, with confidence intervals
rp.predict_median(newdata, ci=True, format="polars")
```

