### Expected survival time

`predict_expectation()` works the same way for the Royston-Parmar model, integrating the smooth
spline-based survival curve up to `tau` to give the restricted mean survival time. As with the AFT
models, `tau` is required and must be specified explicitly.

::: {#f1a467f6 .cell execution_count=32}
``` {.python .cell-code}
# Expected survival time (RMST) up to 365 days for each subject
rp.predict_expectation(newdata, tau=365, format="polars")
```

