Comparing the three plots side by side tells you which distributional family linearizes the data
best. This visual approach complements the AIC comparison from `compare_distributions()` and the
likelihood ratio tests from `test_distributions()`.

::: {.callout-tip}
## Weibull plot + AIC = confidence in your distribution choice

Use `compare_distributions()` or `test_distributions()` for a numeric answer and `plot_weibull()`
for the visual confirmation. If AIC picks Weibull and the Weibull plot is linear, you can proceed
with confidence. If the numbers and the picture disagree, investigate further.
:::

## Next steps

You can now fit, compare, predict from, and diagnose parametric survival models.

- [Cox model diagnostics](cox-diagnostics.qmd) covers residuals and influence diagnostics for
the semiparametric alternative, with the same conceptual framework.
- [Cox regression](cox-regression.qmd) is the semiparametric alternative, useful when you
prefer not to assume a distribution.
- [Prediction performance](prediction-performance.qmd) evaluates any fitted model,
parametric or not.
- [Competing risks](competing-risks.qmd) handles the case of more than one type of event.
